column6:
Here's another neat example of short-circuit or:<p><pre><code>    function getFoo(f) {
        if (f) {
            if (foos[f]) {
                return foos[f];
            } else {
                return f;
            }
        } else {
            return "error";
        }
    }
</code></pre>
Is (almost) the same as...<p><pre><code>    function getFoo(f) {
        return foos[f] || f || "error";
    }
</code></pre>
The difference in behavior being if foos[undefined] is set...
